From 853cc42f9ac656889ba4361e1ab58834b0dcb443 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SplitMind <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:23:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cloudflare): let MCP OAuth consent choose read-only
 access and accounts

The consent page created every MCP grant with all actions and all connections,
so one client could act as every connected account, including sending mail.
It now asks for Access (read only, the default, or read and write) and an
optional list of account nicknames. After the administrator token is checked,
read-only resolves to the catalog's read actions and nicknames resolve to
connection ids ("alias" on every service, or "service:alias"), and the backing
runtime token is created with that grant. Accounts are never listed on the page,
so an anonymous visitor learns nothing. A nickname that matches nothing is
refused before the consent handle is spent, so the operator can go back and fix it.
